|* Post-layout ro_ring5: the four-ring wstv frequency ladder, extracted
|* parasitics vs. the pre-layout netlist, in ONE deck.
|*
|* Purpose (issue #22, acceptance criterion 2). Every ro_ring5 number this
|* repo has recorded so far comes from design/*.spice -- xschem's own
|* schematic export, with no physical interconnect in it at all. This deck
|* re-runs the same measurement against layout/pex/ro_ring5_pex.spice, the
|* `klt extract --parasitics` netlist of the composed, DRC-clean and
|* LVS-clean cells under layout/ (layout/bin/pex-netlist.py builds it from
|* the committed GDS; layout/pex/README.md states exactly what its parasitic
|* model contains).
|*
|* Why both rings are in ONE deck rather than compared across two records.
|* The quantity of interest is a RATIO -- how much slower is the same ring
|* once its own intra-cell parasitics are present -- and a ratio taken
|* across two runs silently inherits every difference between them (corner
|* section, temperature, solver settings, ngspice build, the estimator's own
|* start-up transient). Running the pre-layout ring as a same-deck control
|* at the same corner, same temperature, same supply, same timestep and the
|* same measurement code makes the parasitic contribution the ONLY thing
|* that differs between the two numbers this deck prints.
|*
|* Topology. Eight five-stage rings, built in place exactly as
|* design/xschem/ro_ring5.sch wires one (ro_nand2 + 4 x ro_stage), on eight
|* independent supply sources so each ring's own supply current is
|* separately measurable:
|*
|*   p1..p4  POST-LAYOUT, wstv = 0.42 / 0.44 / 0.46 / 0.48 um -- one
|*           physical cell per ring, the four distinct DRC/LVS-clean
|*           layout cells under layout/ro_{stage,nand2}[_wstv0p4x]/.
|*   q1..q4  PRE-LAYOUT control, the identical ladder from
|*           design/ro_array_core.spice's parameterized .subckt.
|*
|* Every ring drives its own output buffer -- a post-layout ro_buf_pex for
|* p1..p4, a pre-layout ro_buf for q1..q4 -- on one block supply per side,
|* so no buffer's current contaminates a ring's own vddr.
|* design/xschem/ro_array_core.sch wires a per-ring output buffer this way,
|* and buffering ALL four rings rather than one is what makes the four
|* periods a comparable ladder (see the buffer block below).
|*
|* The substrate tie. layout/pex/ro_ring5_pex.spice declares the
|* extractor's substrate return node `vsubs` .global, and every
|* net-to-substrate capacitance in every post-layout cell returns to it
|* (see layout/bin/pex-netlist.py's docstring, and klayout-tools#1503 for
|* why the extractor's own per-instance scoping cannot be used as-is). This
|* deck ties it HARD to 0 -- the physically-motivated choice, since every
|* composed cell carries its own psub guard ring tied to vss and vss is 0
|* here. The complementary bound (vsubs left floating on the extractor's own
|* 1 TOhm dc tie, which makes the shared substrate node an inter-ring
|* coupling path) is measured by this slug's sibling testbench,
|* tb_post_layout_substrate_float.spice.
|*
|* PVT: this deck is run at the same four (temp, supply) points
|* sim/ro-ring5-swing-and-current/ used, each bundling the tt/ss/ff process
|* axis into one record:
|*   -40 degC / 1.62 V   the measured entropy-binding corner (ss)
|*    27 degC / 1.80 V   nominal
|*   125 degC / 1.98 V   the worst five-stage ring swing in #10's grid
|*   -40 degC / 1.98 V   the fastest ring measured anywhere in that grid
|*
|* tstop is 160 ns, twice that deck's 80 ns, because the post-layout rings
|* are slower and the period estimator needs 11 rising edges of the SLOWEST
|* ring (wstv = 0.42, post-layout, ss / -40 degC / 1.62 V) to fit inside the
|* window with start-up discarded.
|*
|* This file is a TEMPLATE: sim/bin/corner-run.py substitutes /Users/rwalters/.volare/volare/sky130/versions/c6d73a35f524070e85faff4a6a9eef49553ebc2b/sky130A/libs.tech/combined/sky130.lib.spice,
|* tt, /Users/rwalters/GitHub/sky130-trng/.loom/worktrees/issue-22/design/ro_array_core.spice, /Users/rwalters/GitHub/sky130-trng/.loom/worktrees/issue-22/layout/pex/ro_ring5_pex.spice, -40.0, 1.62 and 5p. As
|* committed it is not a runnable deck.
|
|.option scale=1u
|.lib "/Users/rwalters/.volare/volare/sky130/versions/c6d73a35f524070e85faff4a6a9eef49553ebc2b/sky130A/libs.tech/combined/sky130.lib.spice" tt
|
|* pre-layout subcircuit library (ro_nand2 / ro_stage / ro_buf)
|.include "/Users/rwalters/GitHub/sky130-trng/.loom/worktrees/issue-22/design/ro_array_core.spice"
|* post-layout subcircuit library (ro_*_pex_*), generated from layout/
|.include "/Users/rwalters/GitHub/sky130-trng/.loom/worktrees/issue-22/layout/pex/ro_ring5_pex.spice"
|
|.temp -40.0
|
|* --- substrate return node: hard tie (see header) ----------------------
|Vsub vsubs 0 dc 0
|
|* --- post-layout rings, one physical cell per wstv ---------------------
|Vddrp1 vddrp1 0 dc 1.62
|Venp1 enp1 0 dc 1.62
|xgp1 p1o enp1 p1a vddrp1 0 ro_nand2_pex_wstv0p42
|x1p1 p1a p1b vddrp1 0 ro_stage_pex_wstv0p42
|x2p1 p1b p1c vddrp1 0 ro_stage_pex_wstv0p42
|x3p1 p1c p1d vddrp1 0 ro_stage_pex_wstv0p42
|x4p1 p1d p1o vddrp1 0 ro_stage_pex_wstv0p42
|
|Vddrp2 vddrp2 0 dc 1.62
|Venp2 enp2 0 dc 1.62
|xgp2 p2o enp2 p2a vddrp2 0 ro_nand2_pex_wstv0p44
|x1p2 p2a p2b vddrp2 0 ro_stage_pex_wstv0p44
|x2p2 p2b p2c vddrp2 0 ro_stage_pex_wstv0p44
|x3p2 p2c p2d vddrp2 0 ro_stage_pex_wstv0p44
|x4p2 p2d p2o vddrp2 0 ro_stage_pex_wstv0p44
|
|Vddrp3 vddrp3 0 dc 1.62
|Venp3 enp3 0 dc 1.62
|xgp3 p3o enp3 p3a vddrp3 0 ro_nand2_pex_wstv0p46
|x1p3 p3a p3b vddrp3 0 ro_stage_pex_wstv0p46
|x2p3 p3b p3c vddrp3 0 ro_stage_pex_wstv0p46
|x3p3 p3c p3d vddrp3 0 ro_stage_pex_wstv0p46
|x4p3 p3d p3o vddrp3 0 ro_stage_pex_wstv0p46
|
|Vddrp4 vddrp4 0 dc 1.62
|Venp4 enp4 0 dc 1.62
|xgp4 p4o enp4 p4a vddrp4 0 ro_nand2_pex_wstv0p48
|x1p4 p4a p4b vddrp4 0 ro_stage_pex_wstv0p48
|x2p4 p4b p4c vddrp4 0 ro_stage_pex_wstv0p48
|x3p4 p4c p4d vddrp4 0 ro_stage_pex_wstv0p48
|x4p4 p4d p4o vddrp4 0 ro_stage_pex_wstv0p48
|
|* --- pre-layout control rings, identical ladder ------------------------
|Vddrq1 vddrq1 0 dc 1.62
|Venq1 enq1 0 dc 1.62
|xgq1 q1o enq1 q1a vddrq1 0 ro_nand2 wstv=0.42 lstv=2 cld=0.5f
|x1q1 q1a q1b vddrq1 0 ro_stage wstv=0.42 lstv=2 cld=0.5f
|x2q1 q1b q1c vddrq1 0 ro_stage wstv=0.42 lstv=2 cld=0.5f
|x3q1 q1c q1d vddrq1 0 ro_stage wstv=0.42 lstv=2 cld=0.5f
|x4q1 q1d q1o vddrq1 0 ro_stage wstv=0.42 lstv=2 cld=0.5f
|
|Vddrq2 vddrq2 0 dc 1.62
|Venq2 enq2 0 dc 1.62
|xgq2 q2o enq2 q2a vddrq2 0 ro_nand2 wstv=0.44 lstv=2 cld=0.5f
|x1q2 q2a q2b vddrq2 0 ro_stage wstv=0.44 lstv=2 cld=0.5f
|x2q2 q2b q2c vddrq2 0 ro_stage wstv=0.44 lstv=2 cld=0.5f
|x3q2 q2c q2d vddrq2 0 ro_stage wstv=0.44 lstv=2 cld=0.5f
|x4q2 q2d q2o vddrq2 0 ro_stage wstv=0.44 lstv=2 cld=0.5f
|
|Vddrq3 vddrq3 0 dc 1.62
|Venq3 enq3 0 dc 1.62
|xgq3 q3o enq3 q3a vddrq3 0 ro_nand2 wstv=0.46 lstv=2 cld=0.5f
|x1q3 q3a q3b vddrq3 0 ro_stage wstv=0.46 lstv=2 cld=0.5f
|x2q3 q3b q3c vddrq3 0 ro_stage wstv=0.46 lstv=2 cld=0.5f
|x3q3 q3c q3d vddrq3 0 ro_stage wstv=0.46 lstv=2 cld=0.5f
|x4q3 q3d q3o vddrq3 0 ro_stage wstv=0.46 lstv=2 cld=0.5f
|
|Vddrq4 vddrq4 0 dc 1.62
|Venq4 enq4 0 dc 1.62
|xgq4 q4o enq4 q4a vddrq4 0 ro_nand2 wstv=0.48 lstv=2 cld=0.5f
|x1q4 q4a q4b vddrq4 0 ro_stage wstv=0.48 lstv=2 cld=0.5f
|x2q4 q4b q4c vddrq4 0 ro_stage wstv=0.48 lstv=2 cld=0.5f
|x3q4 q4c q4d vddrq4 0 ro_stage wstv=0.48 lstv=2 cld=0.5f
|x4q4 q4d q4o vddrq4 0 ro_stage wstv=0.48 lstv=2 cld=0.5f
|
|* --- output buffers: one per ring, on a block supply per side ----------
|* EVERY ring is buffered, post-layout and pre-layout alike. This is not
|* decoration: design/xschem/ro_array_core.sch buffers all four rings, and
|* an earlier revision of this deck that buffered only ring 1 made its own
|* ladder metric meaningless -- the buffered ring ran ~18% slower than its
|* unbuffered neighbours purely from the extra load, which reads as ladder
|* span rather than as the loading it is. See sim/post-layout-ro-ring5's
|* entry in sim/README.md.
|Vddp vddp 0 dc 1.62
|xbp1 p1o p1ob vddp 0 ro_buf_pex
|xbp2 p2o p2ob vddp 0 ro_buf_pex
|xbp3 p3o p3ob vddp 0 ro_buf_pex
|xbp4 p4o p4ob vddp 0 ro_buf_pex
|Vddq vddq 0 dc 1.62
|xbq1 q1o q1ob vddq 0 ro_buf
|xbq2 q2o q2ob vddq 0 ro_buf
|xbq3 q3o q3ob vddq 0 ro_buf
|xbq4 q4o q4ob vddq 0 ro_buf
|
|.ic v(p1o)=0 v(p1a)=1.62 v(p1b)=0 v(p1c)=1.62 v(p1d)=0
|.ic v(p2o)=0 v(p2a)=1.62 v(p2b)=0 v(p2c)=1.62 v(p2d)=0
|.ic v(p3o)=0 v(p3a)=1.62 v(p3b)=0 v(p3c)=1.62 v(p3d)=0
|.ic v(p4o)=0 v(p4a)=1.62 v(p4b)=0 v(p4c)=1.62 v(p4d)=0
|.ic v(q1o)=0 v(q1a)=1.62 v(q1b)=0 v(q1c)=1.62 v(q1d)=0
|.ic v(q2o)=0 v(q2a)=1.62 v(q2b)=0 v(q2c)=1.62 v(q2d)=0
|.ic v(q3o)=0 v(q3a)=1.62 v(q3b)=0 v(q3c)=1.62 v(q3d)=0
|.ic v(q4o)=0 v(q4a)=1.62 v(q4b)=0 v(q4c)=1.62 v(q4d)=0
|
|.tran 5p 160n uic
|
|.control
|run
|
|* Period of every ring, from 8 whole periods with the first two rising
|* edges discarded as start-up -- the same estimator
|* sim/ro-ring5-swing-and-current/ uses, so the two campaigns' periods are
|* directly comparable.
|meas tran tp1a when v(p1o)=0.5*1.62 rise=3
|meas tran tp1b when v(p1o)=0.5*1.62 rise=11
|let t_pex_wstv0p42 = (tp1b - tp1a)/8
|meas tran tp2a when v(p2o)=0.5*1.62 rise=3
|meas tran tp2b when v(p2o)=0.5*1.62 rise=11
|let t_pex_wstv0p44 = (tp2b - tp2a)/8
|meas tran tp3a when v(p3o)=0.5*1.62 rise=3
|meas tran tp3b when v(p3o)=0.5*1.62 rise=11
|let t_pex_wstv0p46 = (tp3b - tp3a)/8
|meas tran tp4a when v(p4o)=0.5*1.62 rise=3
|meas tran tp4b when v(p4o)=0.5*1.62 rise=11
|let t_pex_wstv0p48 = (tp4b - tp4a)/8
|
|meas tran tq1a when v(q1o)=0.5*1.62 rise=3
|meas tran tq1b when v(q1o)=0.5*1.62 rise=11
|let t_pre_wstv0p42 = (tq1b - tq1a)/8
|meas tran tq2a when v(q2o)=0.5*1.62 rise=3
|meas tran tq2b when v(q2o)=0.5*1.62 rise=11
|let t_pre_wstv0p44 = (tq2b - tq2a)/8
|meas tran tq3a when v(q3o)=0.5*1.62 rise=3
|meas tran tq3b when v(q3o)=0.5*1.62 rise=11
|let t_pre_wstv0p46 = (tq3b - tq3a)/8
|meas tran tq4a when v(q4o)=0.5*1.62 rise=3
|meas tran tq4b when v(q4o)=0.5*1.62 rise=11
|let t_pre_wstv0p48 = (tq4b - tq4a)/8
|
|* The headline ratio: same ring, same corner, parasitics on vs. off.
|let slowdown_wstv0p42 = t_pex_wstv0p42 / t_pre_wstv0p42
|let slowdown_wstv0p44 = t_pex_wstv0p44 / t_pre_wstv0p44
|let slowdown_wstv0p46 = t_pex_wstv0p46 / t_pre_wstv0p46
|let slowdown_wstv0p48 = t_pex_wstv0p48 / t_pre_wstv0p48
|
|* Ladder span (DR-0003 section 8's skew_span, re-measured post-layout).
|* Stated as slowest/fastest ring under the ladder's expected monotone
|* ordering; the four periods above are printed individually so a reader
|* can confirm that ordering rather than take it on trust.
|let skew_span_pex = t_pex_wstv0p42 / t_pex_wstv0p48
|let skew_span_pre = t_pre_wstv0p42 / t_pre_wstv0p48
|
|* Swing, ring node and buffered output, post-layout and pre-layout.
|* Steady-state window: 20 ns of start-up discarded.
|meas tran vmaxp MAX v(p1o) from=20n to=160n
|meas tran vminp MIN v(p1o) from=20n to=160n
|meas tran vmaxpb MAX v(p1ob) from=20n to=160n
|meas tran vminpb MIN v(p1ob) from=20n to=160n
|meas tran vmaxq MAX v(q1o) from=20n to=160n
|meas tran vminq MIN v(q1o) from=20n to=160n
|meas tran vmaxqb MAX v(q1ob) from=20n to=160n
|meas tran vminqb MIN v(q1ob) from=20n to=160n
|let swing_frac_pex_ring = (vmaxp - vminp) / 1.62
|let swing_frac_pex_buf = (vmaxpb - vminpb) / 1.62
|let swing_frac_pre_ring = (vmaxq - vminq) / 1.62
|let swing_frac_pre_buf = (vmaxqb - vminqb) / 1.62
|
|* Per-ring supply current, running. i(Vsrc) is negative for current
|* delivered by the source, so the printed figures are sign-flipped to read
|* as consumed current.
|meas tran ip1raw AVG i(Vddrp1) from=20n to=160n
|meas tran ip4raw AVG i(Vddrp4) from=20n to=160n
|meas tran iq1raw AVG i(Vddrq1) from=20n to=160n
|meas tran iq4raw AVG i(Vddrq4) from=20n to=160n
|let i_pex_wstv0p42 = -ip1raw
|let i_pex_wstv0p48 = -ip4raw
|let i_pre_wstv0p42 = -iq1raw
|let i_pre_wstv0p48 = -iq4raw
|
|print t_pex_wstv0p42
|print t_pex_wstv0p44
|print t_pex_wstv0p46
|print t_pex_wstv0p48
|print t_pre_wstv0p42
|print t_pre_wstv0p44
|print t_pre_wstv0p46
|print t_pre_wstv0p48
|print slowdown_wstv0p42
|print slowdown_wstv0p44
|print slowdown_wstv0p46
|print slowdown_wstv0p48
|print skew_span_pex
|print skew_span_pre
|print swing_frac_pex_ring
|print swing_frac_pex_buf
|print swing_frac_pre_ring
|print swing_frac_pre_buf
|print i_pex_wstv0p42
|print i_pex_wstv0p48
|print i_pre_wstv0p42
|print i_pre_wstv0p48
|.endc
|.end
|

